#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""herdr-sleep: put Claude agents that have been quiet for a day to sleep, with a summary page.

The claude process exits (its memory and MCP servers go with it), the pane stays, and a page
in it shows what the conversation was about. Enter resumes the same session in the same folder
with the same launch flags. Anything uncertain keeps the agent awake.

  startup                 re-show pages after a Herdr restart, start the watcher
  ensure                  start the watcher unless one runs
  watch                   sweep every POLL_SECONDS (the watcher)
  sweep                   one pass: sleep every agent that qualifies
  preview                 show each agent and why it would or would not sleep
  sleep-pane PANE         sleep one agent now (skips the quiet-time and focus checks)
  list                    sleeping sessions and their manual resume commands
  refresh                 redraw every sleeping page with the current code (after an update)
  page SESSION            the in-pane page; Enter wakes (typed by sleep, not by hand)
  after-wake PANE SESSION give the woken agent its name back, drop the record

Settings: ~/.config/herdr-sleep/config.json (optional; see README). State: ~/.local/state/herdr-sleep/.
"""
